3
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:26.000
This episode involves a crime against children. It may not be suitable for all listeners. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples should be aware that this episode contains the names of people who have passed away. Nestled in the hinterland of mid-north New South Wales is the town of Bowerville, which sits about 20 kilometres inland from the coast.
本期节目涉及针对儿童的犯罪。可能不适合所有听众。原住民和托雷斯海峡岛民应注意，本期节目包含已故人员的姓名。坐落在新南威尔士州中北部腹地的博韦尔维尔（Bowerville）镇，距离海岸约 20 公里。

4
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:56.000
The fertile lands in the surrounding area led to a booming agricultural industry over the years, with farmers raising cattle and growing produce such as bananas, macadamia nuts, and avocados. Bowerville itself was constructed around the timber industry, but the area's natural beauty is equally notable, characterised by rugged bushland. Life around Bowerville has often been described as sleepy,
多年来，周边地区的肥沃土地催生了蓬勃发展的农业，农民们饲养牲畜并种植香蕉、夏威夷果和牛油果等农产品。博韦尔维尔本身是围绕木材产业建立的，但该地区自然风光同样引人注目，其特点是崎岖的灌木林。博韦尔维尔周围的生活经常被形容为沉睡般宁静，

5
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:21.000
with locals more or less keeping to themselves, but eventually city dwellers started moving to the area in search of a tree change. It was easy to see what drew them there. Driving through Bowerville's town centre, it looks like something out of a picture book. Quaint heritage buildings lined the main street, ranging from an art deco-era movie theatre
当地人或多或少安分守己，但最终城里人开始搬到该地区寻找田园生活。不难看出是什么吸引了他们。驾车穿过博韦尔维尔的镇中心，它看起来就像一本图画书里的景象。古朴的遗产建筑排列在主街两旁，从装饰艺术风格的电影院

6
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:54.000
to Victorian-era pubs. In 1990, the town's population numbered around 1,500, but there were really two Bowervilles. The town was home to about 150 indigenous residents, who all too often experienced racism. Most of them lived around an area known as The Mish. Sprawling along a street then called Cemetery Road, now renamed Gumbagya Road,
到维多利亚风格的酒吧。1990年，该镇人口约为1500人，但实际上有两个博韦尔维尔。该镇大约有 150 名原住民居民，他们常常遭受种族歧视。他们大多住在被称为“The Mish”的地区附近。沿着当时名为墓地路（Cemetery Road）、现更名为甘巴贾路（Gumbagya Road）的一条街道延伸，

7
00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:28.000
The Mish was a row of houses on the outskirts of town, away from the gentile-looking buildings that were so attractive to tourists. Its name came from the unofficial Aboriginal mission that had been there between the 1880s and the 1950s. During Australia's civil rights movement in the 1960s, activist Charles Perkins led a freedom bus ride through Bowerville to protest discrimination against Australia's First Nations peoples.
The Mish 是镇郊的一排房屋，远离那些对游客极具吸引力的绅士风格建筑。它的名字来源于1880年代至1950年代期间存在于那里的非官方原住民教会。在20世纪60年代澳大利亚民权运动期间，活动家查尔斯·帕金斯（Charles Perkins）带领自由乘车之旅穿过博韦尔维尔，抗议对澳大利亚第一民族人民的歧视。

8
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Back then, Bowerville's indigenous residents were barred from the cinema, the RSL, the local school, and even the hospital. By 1990, the segregation wasn't this extreme, yet there was still one pub for white people and another for indigenous people. Those who lived in the community at the time have described the racism as palpable.
当时，博韦尔维尔的原住民居民被禁止进入电影院、RSL、当地学校甚至医院。到 1990 年代，隔离已经没有这么极端了，但仍然有一家白人酒吧和另一家原住民酒吧。当时住在该社区的人形容种族歧视是显而易见的。

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:29.000
But long before Bowerville was ever known as Bowerville, the area was home to the Gumbagya people. They are the traditional custodians of lands sprawling across more than 6,000 square kilometres and have their own distinct language, traditions, and stories. One of their stories has been passed down from elders to children as a cautionary tale. It involves a goomba, an evil spirit that prowls along the banks of a river
但在博韦尔维尔被称为博韦尔维尔很久以前，该地区就是甘巴贾（Gumbagya）人民的家园。他们是跨越6000多平方公里土地的传统托管人，拥有自己独特的语言、传统和故事。他们的一个故事作为警世寓言由长辈传给儿童。它涉及一个冈巴（goomba），一个在河岸边徘徊的邪恶精灵，

10
00:04:29.000 --> 00:05:20.000
looking for children to steal. The goomba is a shapeshifter so he can disguise himself amongst others. This way, he doesn't look suspicious and can prey on his victims when they least expect it, or he'll sit up in a tree looking down and plotting his attack. It's said that he most often waits until night time to strike, leading parents to warn their children that they must always be quiet after dark.
寻找要偷走的孩子。冈巴是一个换形者，所以他可以把自己伪装在其他人中间。这样，他就不会显得可疑，并能在受害者最意想不到的时候捕食他们，或者他会坐在树上向下看并策划他的袭击。据说他通常会等到夜幕降临时才出手，导致父母警告他们的孩子们天黑后一定要保持安静。

11
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Tap. Tap. Tap. Muriel Craig heard a gentle knocking at the window as she bustled around her kitchen, cleaning the mess left over from that evening's meal. It was around nine o'clock and completely dark out. Muriel looked up. It sounded like someone was wrapping up and he heard a gentle knocking at the window
叩。叩。叩。穆里尔·克雷格（Muriel Craig）在厨房里忙碌着，清理着当晚饭后留下的残局，这时她听到窗户传来轻柔的敲击声。当时大约九点钟，外面一片漆黑。穆里尔抬起头。听起来有人在包扎，她听到窗户传来轻柔的敲击声

12
00:05:45.000 --> 00:06:18.000
as she bustled around her kitchen, It sounded like someone was wrapping on the window from outside, but she couldn't see anybody standing there. The experience was almost unsettling until Muriel realized the source of the noise. Crouching out of sight outside was her ten-year-old daughter, Colleen. The little girl was tapping against the glass, trying to scare her mother into thinking there was a ghost outside.
当她在厨房里忙碌时，听起来好像有人在外面敲窗户，但她看不到任何人站在那里。这种经历几乎让人不安，直到穆里尔意识到噪音的来源。蹲在外面视线之外的是她十岁的女儿科琳（Colleen）。这个小女孩正敲打着玻璃，想吓唬她母亲，让她以为外面有鬼。

13
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:49.000
The mischievous Colleen had a reputation for being a practical joker. She particularly liked playing tricks on her mum, much to Muriel's amusement. As she got older, Colleen kept her sense of humour while also growing up into a responsible young woman. She helped look after her younger siblings, in particular her brother, who was in a wheelchair and had special needs. Colleen hoped to become a preschool teacher one day,
淘气的科琳以恶作剧闻名。她特别喜欢捉弄她的妈妈，这让穆里尔觉得很有趣。随着年龄的增长，科琳保持了她的幽默感，同时也成长为一个负责任的年轻女性。她帮忙照顾年幼的弟弟妹妹，特别是她那个坐轮椅且有特殊需求的弟弟。科琳希望有一天能成为一名学前班老师，

14
00:06:49.000 --> 00:07:17.000
a profession that her friends and family thought would perfectly suit her caring and playful nature. More than six years after Colleen first played a prank on her mother by tapping on a window, Muriel was once again in the kitchen when she suddenly heard a familiar sound. Tap, tap, tap. This time, the noise upset her.
她的朋友和家人认为这个职业非常适合她富有同情心和顽皮的性格。在科琳第一次通过敲窗户恶作剧捉弄母亲六年多后，穆里尔再次来到厨房，突然听到了熟悉的声音。叩，叩，叩。这一次，噪音让她感到不安。

15
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:48.000
Muriel entered the lounge where her children had gathered and told them off for the practical joke, explaining that they mustn't tap on the window because it was something that Colleen used to do. Muriel's other children insisted that none of them had been outside. They had all been in the lounge the entire time. Their faces were serious and Muriel believed them. Yet, it couldn't have been Colleen either.
穆里尔走进孩子们聚集的客厅，训斥了他们的恶作剧，并解释说他们绝不能敲窗户，因为那是科琳过去常常做的事。穆里尔的其他孩子坚持说他们中没有一个人去过外面。他们整时间都在客厅里。他们的表情很严肃，穆里尔相信了他们。然而，也不可能是科琳。

16
00:07:48.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Colleen, who was now 16 years old, had recently disappeared. Her distraught family had searched tirelessly for her to no avail. As it was clear no one else was responsible for the tapping, Muriel felt certain of one thing. It was her daughter's spirit reaching out, letting her know she was there. Colleen Craig had been excited as she packed her bags in preparation for a holiday.
现年 16 岁的科琳最近失踪了。她心烦意乱的家人不知疲倦地寻找她，但无济于事。由于很明显没有人对敲门声负责，穆里尔确信一件事。那是她女儿的灵魂在联系，让她知道她在那里。科琳·克雷格（Colleen Craig）在收拾行李准备度假时感到非常兴奋。

17
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:52.000
The teenager was eager to start exploring the world and embrace life as a young adult. She lived with her mother and siblings in the New South Wales town of Sortel, but recently she'd taken a couple of trips to visit family in Bowerville, almost 58km away. Now she was going one step further by travelling with friends. Colleen and three other girls planned to leave Bowerville
这个十几岁的女孩渴望开始探索世界，并以年轻人的身份拥抱生活。她和母亲及兄弟姐妹住在新南威尔士州的索特尔（Sortel）镇，但最近她曾几次去拜访住在近 58 公里外的博韦尔维尔的家人。现在，她要和朋友一起旅行，迈出更远的一步。科琳和另外三个女孩计划离开博韦尔维尔

18
00:08:52.000 --> 00:09:31.000
on the night of September 13, 1990 to catch a 3am train to Sydney. They were headed for the town of Goduga near the Queensland border. It was a long journey with a late start. After she finished packing, Colleen headed over to a party at the Mish, where most of Bowerville's indigenous residents lived. Across the road was a small park where a campfire had been set up for the party. Attendees mingled around the fire and over the road, in the home of a local resident named Marjorie Jarrett.
1990年9月13日晚，赶搭凌晨3点开往悉尼的火车。他们的目的地是靠近昆士兰州边境的戈杜加（Goduga）镇。这是一段漫长的旅程，出发时间很晚。收拾好行李后，科琳前往 Mish 的一个派对，博韦尔维尔的大多数原住民居民都住在那里。马路对面是一个小公园，为派对搭起了篝火。参与者在火堆周围以及马路对面、当地居民玛乔丽·贾雷特（Marjorie Jarrett）的家中来回穿梭。

19
00:09:31.000 --> 00:10:23.000
They also spilled out into a laneway that sat alongside Marjorie's house. Colleen was spotted numerous times throughout the afternoon and evening. Sometimes she sat inside the lounge room and chatted with friends. Other times she was seen with a group gathered beneath a large gum tree in the park opposite. They were drinking beer and Colleen appeared somewhat intoxicated. At around midnight, Colleen was spotted walking down the alleyway alongside Marjorie's house. Hours later, Colleen's three travel companions were preparing to leave for the train station. Marjorie Jarrett had offered to drive the group and searched for Colleen in and around the party with no success.
他们还涌入紧邻玛乔丽房屋的一条小巷。整个下午和晚上，人们多次看到科琳的身影。有时她坐在客厅里与朋友聊天。有时人们看到她和一群人聚集在对面公园的一棵大桉树下。他们当时在喝啤酒，科琳看起来有点醉了。午夜左右，有人看到科琳沿着玛乔丽房屋旁的小巷走去。几小时后，科琳的三个旅伴正准备前往火车站。玛乔丽·贾雷特曾主动提出开车送这群人，并在派对内外寻找科琳，但没有成功。

20
00:10:23.000 --> 00:11:13.000
In the end, Colleen's friends left for their holiday without her. The 3am train to Sydney departed without Colleen on board. As soon as word reached Muriel Craig that her daughter hadn't gone on her trip as planned and hadn't been seen since the party, she knew that something was terribly wrong. Muriel travelled from her home in Sautel to Barreville so she could report Colleen missing. All of the officers at Barreville police station were white. The two who Muriel reported to were dubious when she showed them a picture of Colleen. Noting that the teenage girl had lighter skin than her mother, the officers remarked,
最后，科琳的朋友们在没有她的情况下踏上了假期。开往悉尼的凌晨 3 点的火车出发了，科琳却没有登车。一听到穆里尔·克雷格得知她的女儿没有按计划去旅行，并且自派对以来就再也没有露面，她就知道出大事了。穆里尔从她在索特尔的家赶到巴雷维尔（Barreville），以便她可以报告科琳失踪。巴雷维尔警察局的所有警官都是白人。穆里尔向其中两名警官报案时，他们看了科琳的照片后表现得很怀疑。注意到这个十几岁的女孩皮肤比她母亲白，警官们评论道，

21
00:11:13.000 --> 00:12:22.000
she don't look aboriginal to us and asked if she was really Muriel's daughter. Then they suggested that perhaps Colleen had simply, quote, gone walkabout. In Australia's indigenous cultures, walkabout is a rite of passage in which adolescent males live alone in the wilderness for a period of time. The term has become twisted and misused by non-indigenous people who see aboriginal people as living transient nomadic lifestyles. Some used the word walkabout in a derogatory sense to imply an indigenous person has just taken off on a whim without warning. Muriel was devastated by the policemen's comments and retorted. I wouldn't be silly enough to come in here and report her missing. I am not that stupid. But the officers remained disinterested and unwilling to take a report, remarking that Colleen would probably turn up soon enough.
她看起来不像我们的原住民，并问她是否真的是穆里尔的女儿。然后他们暗示科琳可能只是“去漫游（walkabout）”了。在澳大利亚的原住民文化中，漫游是青春期男性在荒野中独自生活一段时间的成人礼。这个术语被非原住民扭曲和滥用，他们将原住民视为过着短暂游牧生活方式的人。一些人以贬义的方式使用“漫游”一词，暗示原住民在没有任何警告的情况下凭一时冲动离开。穆里尔对警察的言论感到痛心并反驳道。我不会傻到跑来这里报告她失踪。我没那么蠢。但警察仍然表现得漠不关心，不愿立案，并表示科琳可能很快就会出现。

22
00:12:22.000 --> 00:13:33.000
Muriel handed over her photograph of Colleen for their reference, then left the station. With no help from law enforcement, Colleen's family took on the responsibility of finding her. Muriel moved her other children down to Barreville so she could keep searching for Colleen while keeping everyone together. With the help of some relatives, Muriel searched the surrounding areas and spoke to everyone they could find who had been at the party. The police never made any attempt to contact her. Exactly three weeks after Colleen vanished, another party was in full swing at the Mish. This time, the get-together was at Patricia Stadham's house, three doors down from where the previous party had been held. Patricia's daughter Rebecca, who was in her early 20s and lived there too, took her young children over to her ex-partner's house so he could mind them while she was at the party.
穆里尔交出了科琳的照片供他们参考，然后离开了警察局。在没有执法部门帮助的情况下，科琳的家人承担起了寻找她的责任。穆里尔把她其他的孩子搬到了巴雷维尔，这样她就可以继续寻找科琳，同时把大家聚在一起。在一些亲戚的帮助下，穆里尔搜寻了周边地区，并与他们能找到的、参加过派对的所有人进行了交谈。警方从未试图联系她。在科琳失踪整整三 weeks 后，Mish 又举行了一场派对。这一次，聚会在帕特里夏·斯塔达姆（Patricia Stadham）的房子里举行，距离上次派对举行的地方隔了三扇门。帕特里夏的女儿丽贝卡（Rebecca）二十出头，也住在那里，她把自己的幼子带到了前伴侣的房子里，这样他可以在她去派对时照顾他们。

23
00:13:33.000 --> 00:14:44.000
Rebecca and Billy Greenup had a four-year-old daughter named Evelyn, as well as two younger boys Aidan and Aaron. Rebecca was dismayed to discover that Billy was too drunk to look after their young children, so she took them back to her mother's house. After socializing with the party guests, Rebecca decided to go to bed. She slept in the same room as her three children, with four-year-old Evelyn nestled beside her. Rebecca fell asleep fully dressed and didn't wake at all during the night, which was unusual. As soon as she opened her eyes the following morning, Rebecca felt extremely sick in an unfamiliar way. She sat up. Her two sons, Aidan and Aaron, were awake and quietly playing together, but there was no sign of Evelyn. Evelyn and Aaron were very close and rarely left each other's sides, so her absence struck Rebecca as particularly strange.
丽贝卡和比利·格林纳普（Billy Greenup）有一个四岁的女儿伊芙琳（Evelyn），还有两个年幼的男孩艾丹（Aidan）和亚伦（Aaron）。丽贝卡惊恐地发现比利喝得太多，无法照顾他们的幼子，于是她把他们带回了母亲家。与派对客人社交后，丽贝卡决定上床睡觉。她和三个孩子睡在同一个房间里，四岁的伊芙琳依偎在她身旁。丽贝卡和衣入睡，整晚都没有醒来，这很不寻常。第二天一早一睁开眼睛，丽贝卡就感到一种不寻常的极度不适。她坐起身来。她的两个儿子艾丹和亚伦已经醒了，正静静地一起玩耍，但不见伊芙琳的踪影。伊芙琳和亚伦关系非常好，很少离开彼此身边，所以她的缺席让丽贝卡感到格外奇怪。

24
00:14:44.000 --> 00:16:07.000
She asked her boys if they knew where their sister was, but they just looked back at her, wide-eyed and silent. Wondering if Evelyn had wandered off to visit her father, who lived just a few doors down the street, Rebecca first checked at Billy Greenup's house. Evelyn wasn't there, nor was she at any other house in the Mish. Rebecca expanded her search to the centre of Barreville. No one she spoke to had seen Evelyn since the previous night, before the little girl had gone to bed alongside her mother and siblings. Rebecca's panic grew. By mid-morning she was back at home, scouring the surroundings for any sign of her daughter. Suddenly she found something. Lying in the front yard was a single pink sand shoe. It belonged to Evelyn. As word spread about the missing child, an incident that had occurred the previous night took on a sinister new tone. Rebecca's mother Patricia recalled that she'd been woken at around 3am by the sound of Evelyn crying.
她问儿子们是否知道妹妹在哪里，但他们只是睁大眼睛看着她，沉默不语。丽贝卡想知道伊芙琳是否溜出去看望住在街头几步之遥的父亲，于是她首先去了比利·格林纳普的家。伊芙琳不在那里，Mish 的其他房子里也没有她。丽贝卡将搜索范围扩大到巴雷维尔的中心。她与之交谈过的任何人自前一晚小女孩上床睡觉和母亲及兄弟姐妹在一起后就再也没见过她。丽贝卡的恐慌加剧了。到上午中旬，她已经回到家里，在周围寻找女儿的踪迹。突然她发现了一些东西。前院里躺着一只粉红色的沙滩鞋。它属于伊芙琳。随着失踪儿童的消息传开，前一晚发生的一起事件呈现出一种险恶的新基调。丽贝卡的母亲帕特里夏回忆说，她在大约凌晨 3 点被伊芙琳的哭声吵醒。

25
00:16:07.000 --> 00:17:15.000
She got up to check on her, walking down the hall to the room where Evelyn, Rebecca and the two boys were sleeping. The door was closed so Patricia went to open it, but it wouldn't budge. Then she heard a thud, almost like a window being shut, and Evelyn stopped crying. Assuming the little girl had gone back to sleep, Patricia returned to her own room. By evening, Rebecca and her sister Michelle had arrived at the Barreville police station to report Evelyn missing. There was just one officer on duty. Michelle explained the situation and handed the officer a photo. It showed Evelyn with her blue eyes and mop of light brown ringlets, which many people had compared to the hair of famous child actress Shirley Temple. The officer replied,
她起身去查看情况，顺着走廊走到伊芙琳、丽贝卡和两个男孩睡觉的房间。门是关着的，所以帕特里夏去开门，但门纹丝不动。然后她听到“咚”的一声，几乎像是窗户关上的声音，伊芙琳不哭了。帕特里夏以为小女孩又睡着了，便回到了自己的房间。到了傍晚，丽贝卡和她的妹妹米歇尔（Michelle）来到了巴雷维尔警察局报告伊芙琳失踪。当时值班的只有一名警官。米歇尔解释了情况并交给警官一张照片。照片上是伊芙琳，她有一双蓝色的眼睛和一头浅棕色卷曲的头发，许多人将其与著名童星秀兰·邓波儿的头发相提并论。警官回答说，

26
00:17:15.000 --> 00:18:29.000
What do you want me to do? I'm the only one here and I'm just about to go home. Stunned, Michelle repeated that she wanted to report Evelyn missing, explaining that she was just four years old. But the officer wouldn't budge, and it took several more days before Evelyn's family successfully filed a missing persons report. Just as they'd done when Colleen went missing, the police suggested that Evelyn might have, quote, gone walkabout. Yet, they also questioned her indigenous heritage by pointing out her fair skin and blue eyes. Despite taking statements, the police didn't send anybody out to look for Evelyn, and initially her family were left to search for her alone. They called everyone they knew, plastered the town with flyers, and searched high and low through bushland. As so many people had been drinking and partying on the night Evelyn disappeared, it was difficult to piece together what exactly had gone on that night.
你想让我做什么？我是这里唯一的人，我正准备回家。米歇尔惊呆了，重复说她想报告伊芙琳失踪，并解释说她只有四岁。但这名警官态度坚决，又过了好几天，伊芙琳的家人才成功提交了失踪人员报告。就像科琳失踪时一样，警方暗示伊芙琳可能“去漫游了”。然而，他们还通过指出她白皙的皮肤和蓝色的眼睛来质疑她的原住民血统。尽管做了笔录，但警方并没有派任何人出去寻找伊芙琳，最初她的家人只能独自寻找她。他们给认识的所有人打电话，在全镇贴满传单，并在灌木林中上下搜寻。由于许多人在伊芙琳失踪当晚都在喝酒和聚会，很难拼凑出当晚到底发生了什么。

27
00:18:29.000 --> 00:19:34.000
Nevertheless, they knew that she hadn't simply wandered off somewhere. Evelyn was a shy child, who stayed close to her family and was scared of strangers. Three days after Evelyn vanished, the police finally began searching for her, along with volunteers from the local state emergency services. They looked in the nearby Nambucco River and the scrubby bushland that surrounded Bowerville. There was no sign of her. When investigators finally started interviewing people in relation to the case, it was clear that their suspicions fell exclusively on those closest to Evelyn. Her grandmother, Patricia, was interrogated about money that had been transferred into her bank account, with police implying that she and Rebecca had sold Evelyn. In reality, the payments Patricia had received were from her War Widow's pension.
然而，他们知道她并不是随便漫无目的地走开。伊芙琳是一个害羞的孩子，她总是紧紧跟着家人，害怕陌生人。伊芙琳失踪三天后，警方终于开始搜寻她，当地州紧急服务部门的志愿者也加入了搜寻行列。他们在附近的纳姆布科河（Nambucca River）和环绕博韦尔维尔的灌木丛中寻找。没有她的踪迹。当调查人员最终开始就此案对人们进行讯问时，很明显，他们的怀疑完全落在了与伊芙琳最亲近的人身上。她的祖母帕特里夏因转入她银行账户的资金而受到审讯，警方暗示她和丽贝卡把伊芙琳卖了。实际上，帕特里夏收到的款项来自她的战争遗孀抚恤金。

28
00:19:34.000 --> 00:20:41.000
It was also evident that the police had no understanding of indigenous family dynamics, which are more community focused. Because Rebecca had been drinking on the night Evelyn vanished, they assumed her children weren't being looked after. In reality, a wider circle of aunts would always help young parents care for their children. Some news outlets began to pick up the story of the missing four-year-old. When speaking to journalists, the Bowerville police sergeant was adamant. There was absolutely no connection between Evelyn Greenup and the recent disappearance of 16-year-old Colleen Craig. By December of 1990, summer had arrived and brought with it a new resident. Clinton's speedy duro was a 16-year-old boy who had moved from Queensland to Bowerville to live with his father, Thomas Duro.
这也显现出警方根本不了解原住民家庭动态，因为原住民家庭更具社区凝聚力。由于丽贝卡在伊芙琳失踪当晚喝了酒，他们便认为她的孩子没有受到照顾。实际上，更广泛的阿姨圈子总是会帮助年轻父母照顾孩子。一些新闻媒体开始关注这个四岁儿童失踪的故事。在与记者交谈时，博韦尔维尔的警长态度坚决。伊芙琳·格林纳普与 16 岁科琳·克雷格最近的失踪事件之间绝对没有任何联系。到 1990 年 12 月，夏天已经来临，并带来了一位新居民。16 岁的少年克林顿·斯比迪·迪罗（Clinton Speedy Duro）从昆士兰搬到博韦尔维尔，与他的父亲托马斯·迪罗（Thomas Duro）同住。

29
00:20:41.000 --> 00:21:47.000
A sharp dresser who loved footy and had a kind, happy-go-lucky personality, it didn't take long for Clinton to make friends. In particular, he became close to Kelly Jarrett, a teenage girl who had been good friends with Colleen Craig. Clinton and Kelly soon became an item and were rarely seen out of each other's company. On the night of January 31, 1991, the young couple attended a party that was being held around the corner from the Mish, in a public housing flat situated on Herbourne Drive. Rather than go to their respective homes when they were ready to leave, Clinton and Kelly decided to sleep in the yellow Viscount Caravan of a friend. Clinton took off his shoes and the couple watched music videos for a little while, before falling asleep on the same double bed sometime after 3am. Kelly slept soundly. When she woke up, it was 8.40 in the morning.
克林顿衣着时髦，热爱澳式橄榄球，性格善良、随和，没过多久他就交到了朋友。特别是，他与凯利·贾雷特（Kelly Jarrett）走得很近，这是一个曾与科琳·克雷格是好朋友的十几岁女孩。克林顿和凯利很快就成了一对恋人，形影不离。1991年1月31日晚，这对年轻的情侣参加了一个在Mish拐角处、位于赫伯恩大道（Herbourne Drive）的公共住房公寓里举行的派对。准备离开时，克林顿和凯利没有各自回家，而是决定睡在一个朋友的黄色维康大篷车（Viscount Caravan）里。克林顿脱下鞋子，两人看了一会儿音乐录影带，然后在凌晨 3 点之后的某个时间睡在同一张双人床上。凯利睡得很熟。她醒来时，已经是早上 8 点 40 分。

30
00:21:47.000 --> 00:22:38.000
There was no sign of Clinton. Perhaps he'd woken up earlier and already gone home. But then Kelly saw something on the floor of the van, Clinton's Reebok sneakers. Clinton always took pride in his outfits and paid particular attention to his shoes. He never went anywhere barefoot. His father had given him the Reeboks as a Christmas present and Clinton loved them. In his family, it was a source of amusement that he wore them at all times. If Clinton had left already, it made no sense that he'd leave his Reeboks behind. Kelly picked up her boyfriend's shoes and exited the caravan, heading for Clinton's father's house.
没有克林顿的踪影。也许他醒得早，已经回家了。但接着凯利看到大篷车地板上有一样东西——克林顿的锐步运动鞋。克林顿总是为自己的穿着感到自豪，并且特别注意自己的鞋子。他从不光脚去任何地方。他的父亲送给他一双锐步作为圣诞礼物，克林顿非常喜欢它们。在他们家里，他随时随地穿着这双鞋成了一件趣事。如果克林顿已经离开，他把锐步留在身后就说不通了。凯利拿起男友的鞋子，走出大篷车，走向克林顿父亲的家。

31
00:22:38.000 --> 00:23:37.000
Thomas Duro was surprised when he opened his front door to see his son's girlfriend holding Clinton's Reeboks out in front of her. Clinton wasn't at home and the sight of the shoes he was never seen without was immediately alarming. Thomas phoned the police to see if they could do anything to help find Clinton, but they said they couldn't get involved until he'd been missing for at least 24 hours. So, Thomas set out by himself to search for his son. As he did an owner car, he instead walked all over town. First he went to the flats where the party was held the night before, then he visited the caravan where Clinton had spent the night. There was no sign of him anywhere. Thomas checked the town's pubs and other social areas, but nobody he spoke to had seen Clinton since the party.
托马斯·迪罗打开前门，看到儿子的女朋友手里拿着克林顿的锐步鞋伸向前方时，感到非常惊讶。克林顿不在家，看到这双他从不离脚的鞋子立刻让人感到警惕。托马斯打电话给警方，看他们是否能做点什么来帮忙寻找克林顿，但他们说在克林顿失踪至少 24 小时之前他们不能介入。于是，托马斯独自出发去寻找他的儿子。由于他没有车，他只能在全镇步行搜寻。首先他去了前一晚举行派对的公寓，然后他参观了克林顿过夜的大篷车。到处都没有他的踪迹。托马斯检查了镇上的酒吧和其他社交场所，但与他交谈的人中没有人自派对以来见过克林顿。

32
00:23:37.000 --> 00:24:41.000
As the teenager had only just moved to Bowerville, he didn't know many of its residents and there was nowhere obvious he would have visited. Eventually, Thomas decided that all he could do was go home in the hope that Clinton would turn up. He waited and waited, but Clinton never arrived. When the 24 hour time limit had passed, Thomas tried calling the police again to report his son missing. They were in no hurry to respond, waiting another full day before they paid Thomas a visit at home. As Clinton was 16 years old and strongly built, they suspected he'd simply taken off by himself. His family tried to explain to them the significance of Clinton's shoes being left behind, but the officers couldn't understand how this indicated foul play. All they said was, we'll keep an eye out for him.
由于这个少年刚刚搬到博韦尔维尔，他不认识这里的许多居民，也没有他明显会去拜访的地方。最后，托马斯决定他能做的只有回家，祈祷克林顿会出现。他等啊等，但克林顿从未出现。当 24 小时期限过后，托马斯再次尝试打电话给警方报告他儿子失踪。他们并不着急回应，又等了整整一天才去托马斯家拜访。由于克林顿 16 岁且身材健硕，他们怀疑他只是自己一个人跑了。他的家人试图向他们解释克林顿把鞋子留在身后的重要性，但警官们无法理解这如何表明存在谋杀行为。他们所说的一切就是，“我们会留意他”。

33
00:24:41.000 --> 00:25:48.000
Clinton's aunt began making calls, phoning both the local police and law enforcement in the nearby larger city of Coffs Harbour, begging for assistance. Most of her messages went unanswered, but eventually a liaison officer was sent down from Coffs Harbour to help Clinton's family search the town's streets and surrounding areas. Nothing turned up. Just like Colleen Craig and Evelyn Greenup, Clinton's speedy duro had seemingly vanished from Bowerville. Fear spread through the local Indigenous community. Although the police didn't seem to think the three disappearances were linked, the children's friends and family were certain they were. It was a common thread tying the cases together. Over the course of just five months, all of the children had vanished after attending or being in the vicinity of a party at the Mish.
克林顿的阿姨开始打电话，致电当地警察以及附近大城市科夫斯港（Coffs Harbour）的执法部门，恳求援助。她的绝大多数消息都石沉大海，但最终科夫斯港派出一名联络官前往协助克林顿的家人搜寻镇上的街道和周边地区。一无所获。就像科琳·克雷格和伊芙琳·格林纳普一样，克林顿·斯比迪·迪罗似乎也从博韦尔维尔凭空消失了。恐惧在当地原住民社区蔓延。尽管警方似乎认为这三起失踪案没有关联，但孩子们的亲友却确信它们有关联。这是将这些案件联系在一起的共同线索。在短短五个月的时间里，所有这些儿童都是在参加或身处 Mish 的派对附近后失踪的。

34
00:25:48.000 --> 00:27:04.000
They were sure that Colleen, Evelyn and Clinton had been attacked and weren't merely missing persons. When the documentary Innocence Betrayed, Colleen's aunt Elaine Walker told filmmaker Larissa Burrant that residents around the mission changed their behaviour in response to the disappearances. Many mothers started sleeping in the same room as all of their children, so they could keep an eye on them throughout the night. Where residents had once felt safe, they started locking their doors and windows at all times. When children wanted to go into town, their parents would go with them and they'd walk close together in a tight group. A week after Clinton's disappearance, the community's grief and frustration led to a group of Indigenous residents and several white townsfolk marching on Bowerville's police station in protest. They demanded that action be taken and their children's cases be taken seriously. Behind the scenes, Bowerville police had called in colleagues from the child mistreatment unit in Coffs Harbour.
他们确信科琳、伊芙琳和克林顿遭到了袭击，而不仅仅是失踪人员。在纪录片《背叛的天真》（Innocence Betrayed）中，科琳的阿姨伊莱恩·沃克（Elaine Walker）告诉电影制作人拉里萨·伯兰特（Larissa Burrant），教会周边的居民改变了他们的行为以应对失踪事件。许多母亲开始和她们所有的孩子睡在同一个房间里，这样她们可以在整夜密切关注他们。曾经让居民感到安全的地方，现在他们开始时刻锁上门窗。当孩子们想进城时，他们的父母会陪着他们，紧紧地聚集成一个小组步行。克林顿失踪一周后，社区的悲痛和沮丧导致一群原住民居民和几名白人镇民前往博韦尔维尔警察局进行抗议。他们要求采取行动，并严肃处理他们孩子的案件。幕后，博韦尔维尔警方从科夫斯港的儿童虐待部门请来了同事。

35
00:27:04.000 --> 00:28:21.000
Though they'd initially suggested that the missing trio had just quote, gone walkabout, they were starting to suspect that the families themselves and the Indigenous community more broadly were involved. On February 18, almost three weeks since Clinton's speedy duro had disappeared, two men were hiking through some rugged bushland just outside Bowerville. They were looking for firewood in a rough and tangled area that ran alongside Congarene Road, a dirt road that headed south out of town. As they searched for logs amongst the leafletters scattered across the ground, the two men saw something. It was the badly decomposed remains of Clinton's speedy duro. Clinton was barefoot but still dressed in the clothing he'd been wearing on the night he vanished. He had been dragged through the bushland and the animals had scavenged his body. Lying nearby was a blanket which it seemed he had previously been wrapped in.
尽管他们最初暗示失踪的三人只是“去漫游了”，但他们开始怀疑家庭本身以及更广泛的原住民社区卷入了其中。2月18日，距离克林顿·斯比迪·迪罗失踪将近三周，两名男子正在博韦尔维尔郊外的一些崎岖灌木林中徒步旅行。他们正在一条顺着孔加雷恩路（Congarene Road）延伸的粗糙而杂乱的地区寻找柴火，孔加雷恩路是一条向南通往镇外的土路。当他们在散落着落叶的地面上寻找圆木时，这两个人看到了一些东西。那是克林顿·斯比迪·迪罗严重腐烂的遗体。克林顿赤脚，但仍然穿着他失踪当晚穿的衣服。他曾被拖过灌木林，动物们啃食了他的尸体。附近躺着一条毯子，看起来他以前曾被裹在里面。

36
00:28:21.000 --> 00:29:20.000
The area where he had been dumped was also close to a crop of cannabis. An autopsy revealed that Clinton had died from a severe blow to the head. His jaw had been broken and he'd also been stabbed multiple times. Now investigators had to accept that the young man had met with foul play. Two months later on April 17, a man was fishing in the Nambucca River by the southern end of Congarene Road and just down a slight slope from where Clinton had been found. When something snagged his fishing line, he reeled it in. On the end was a pair of jeans and a belt, heavy and soaking wet as they hung off the line. These items were identified as belonging to Colleen Craig.
他被抛弃的地方也靠近一处大麻种植区。尸检显示，克林顿头部遭受重击身亡。他的下巴骨折了，身上还被刺了多刀。现在调查人员不得不接受这个年轻人遭遇不测的事实。两个月后的4月17日，一名男子在孔加雷恩路南端附近的楠布卡河（Nambucca River）钓鱼，距离发现克林顿的地方只有一段微小的下坡。当有什么东西勾住他的钓鱼线时，他把线卷了上来。线上挂着一条牛仔裤和一条皮带，沉甸甸的，挂在在线上还湿漉漉的。这些物品被确认属于科琳·克雷格。

37
00:29:20.000 --> 00:30:15.000
She had been wearing them on the last night anyone had seen her. Police divers subsequently searched the river. By April 20, they had found four plastic bags that had been weighed down in the river. These contained more of Colleen's clothing, including a cable knit jumper she was last seen in. But there was no sign of Colleen herself. A week later on April 27, the police received a phone call from some concerned locals. They had noticed an unpleasant odour in the bushland alongside Congarene Road and were worried given the recent discoveries in the area. The location was three kilometres away from where Clinton's speedy duro was found.
那是任何人最后一次见到她时她穿的衣服。随后警方潜水员搜查了这条河。到 4 月 20 日，他们已经在河里找到了四个被沉重物体压住的塑料袋。这些袋子里装着更多科琳的衣服，包括她最后一次露面时穿的一件粗电缆针织套头衫。但没有科琳本人的踪迹。一周后的 4 月 27 日，警方接到一些热心当地居民的电话。他们注意到孔加雷恩路旁边的灌木林里有一种令人不快的气味，鉴于该地区最近的发现，他们感到很担心。这个地点距离发现克林顿·斯比迪·迪罗的地方有三公里远。

38
00:30:15.000 --> 00:31:23.000
When searches went out there, they discovered the skeletal remains of a small child. It was Evelyn Greenup. A pink sand shoe was recovered near her body, a match to the other shoe her mother had found in the front yard of her home after Evelyn disappeared. Markson Evelyn's skull confirmed that she too had been killed by a heavy blow to the head. The discovery of Clinton and Evelyn's bodies and the clothing belonging to Colleen left Bowerville reeling. The indigenous community in particular was certain that all three of them had fallen prey to a serial killer. There were too many similarities to ignore from the circumstances of their disappearances right down to where their remains and belongings were found. And both Evelyn and Clinton had been killed by fatal blows to the head.
当搜寻人员前往那里时，他们发现了幼儿的骨骼遗骸。那是伊芙琳·格林纳普。在她的尸体附近找到了一只粉红色的沙滩鞋，与她母亲在伊芙琳失踪后在前院找到的另一只鞋相配。伊芙琳头骨上的标志证实，她也是头部受到重击身亡的。克林顿和伊芙琳尸体的发现以及属于科琳的衣服让博韦尔维尔震动。原住民社区尤其确信这三人全都沦为了连串杀人犯的牺牲品。从他们失踪的情况一直到发现他们遗骸和物品的地方，有太多的相似之处不容忽视。而且伊芙琳和克林顿都是头部遭受致命打击身亡。

39
00:31:23.000 --> 00:32:51.000
A homicide investigation was launched with Detective Sergeant Alan Williams at the helm. The detective had no prior homicide experience but was to be assisted by local investigators and other detectives from the North Region Major Crime Squad. Some of the town's white residents queried the amount of resources the investigation was being given with one person remarking to a journalist from the age newspaper. I wonder whether three missing white children would get the same attention. Although Detective Williams had no experience investigating murders, Clinton's remains contained a pivotal clue. A pillowcase that had been pushed down into his shorts. 25-year-old J. Thomas Hart worked at a tanning factory and was reasonably tall at six feet with a stocky but strong 105 kilogram build. Hart wasn't indigenous but he was known to hang out at the Mish and supplied alcohol and cannabis known to locals as Yanni to the young people who lived there.
