01:04:33.000 --> 01:06:02.000
Now, someone who had been acquitted could be retrialed if fresh and compelling evidence was found. The strike force got back to work and began investigating again. They established that witness sightings of Clinton and Evelyn the morning after they went missing were not correct, and that people had either confused their dates, been mistaken, or were misremembering things. As part of their re-investigation, the strike force also uncovered a crucial piece of information that had been completely ignored until now. At around 5am on the morning of February 1, 1991, delivery drivers Greg Innes and Michael Scaffidi were driving towards Bowerville. They had a load of meat to drop off at the town butcher, and the road stretched out in front of them, dim in the pre-dawn hours. The bright headlights of their truck cast a strong light across their path, while their surroundings faded into darkness. Travelling at a speed of about 80km per hour, the men swung left as they came to a corner on that side, a stretch of road known locally as Norco Corner.
现在，如果发现了新的且令人信服的证据，曾经被判无罪的人可以被重新审判。打击小组重新开始工作，并开始再次调查。他们确定，证人在克林顿和伊芙琳失踪第二天早上看到他们的目击并不是正确的，人们要么搞错了日期，要么弄错了，要么记错了事情。作为重新调查的一部分，打击小组还发现了一个直到现在完全被忽视的关键信息。1991年2月1日凌晨5点左右，送货司机格雷格·英尼斯和迈克尔·斯卡菲迪正开车前往鲍尔维尔。他们有一车肉要送到镇上的肉店，破晓前的几个小时里，道路在他们面前延伸，昏暗不明。卡车耀眼的车头灯在他们的前路上投下了强光，而周围的环境则漸漸隐入黑暗。以大约每小时80公里的速度行驶时，这几个人在转弯处向左转，这段路当地人称为诺科角。

70
01:06:02.000 --> 01:06:55.000
It was then that their truck's high beams illuminated something. A young indigenous man was lying on the road. He had the smooth and youthful face of a teenager, and had a shirt tied around his waist. There were no shoes on his feet. One hand was stretched above his head, which was turned to one side, and he was completely still. As Michael later told the Sydney Morning Herald, it looked like he was either asleep, drunk, or dead. Watch out, there's some guy on the road, he warned Greg. The two men pulled over and parked the truck, then peered out of the window at the person sprawled across the road.
正是在那时，他们的卡车远光灯照亮了某些东西。一个年轻的土著男子躺在路上。他有着青少年般光滑年轻的脸庞，腰上系着一件衬衫。他的脚上没有鞋子。一只手举在头顶上方，头偏向一边，他一动不动。正如迈克尔后来对《悉尼先驱晨报》所说的那样，他看起来要么是睡着了、喝醉了，要么就是死了。“小心，路上有个家伙，”他警告格雷格。这两个人把车停在路边，然后透过车窗向横卧在路上的那个人望去。

71
01:06:55.000 --> 01:07:45.000
They saw there was also a stocky white man at the scene, and he was standing over the boy as though to help him. Leaning across from the passenger seat, Michael asked, Mate, what's going on? We could have hit that guy, he's lying in the middle of the road. The white man reassured Michael and Greg that everything was fine. The indigenous boy was just asleep, and he'd called the police to pick him up. Michael checked whether the man wanted some help in carrying the teenager off the road, but the man waved him off, saying he could manage by himself. Believing the situation was under control, the two delivery men pulled back onto the road and continued on their way.
他们看到现场还有一个身材魁梧的白人男子，他站在那个男孩上方，好像要帮他一样。迈克尔从副驾驶座位探过身去问：“伙计，怎么回事？我们差点撞到那家伙，他躺在路中间。”那名白人男子向迈克尔和格雷格保证一切都好。那个土著男孩只是睡着了，他已经叫了警察来接他。迈克尔查看那个人是否需要帮忙把少年抬离道路，但那个人挥手示意他离开，说他自己能应付。两个送货员相信局势已经得到控制，便把车开回路上，继续他们的行程。

72
01:07:45.000 --> 01:08:35.000
Up ahead, they noticed what looked like a mustard-coloured station wagon parked to one side. Its boot was open, and its lights were off. When Greg and Michael later heard that a 16-year-old named Clinton Speedy Juro had been found murdered in some nearby bushland, they realised the significance of what they had seen. The morning that they had seen a seemingly unconscious indigenous boy lying on the ground was the same day that Clinton was believed to have been attacked. Perhaps the boy's killer had been hoping that a vehicle would run over the body, making it look like an accident instead of murder.
前方，他们注意到一辆看起来像芥末色的旅行车停在一边。它的后备箱开着，车灯关着。当格雷格和迈克尔后来听说一个名叫克林顿·斯皮迪·杜罗的16岁男孩被发现谋杀在附近的灌木丛中时，他们意识到了他们所见所闻的重要性。他们看到一个看似失去知觉的土著男孩躺在地上的那天早晨，正是克林顿被认为遭到袭击的日子。也许男孩的凶手曾希望一辆车会碾过尸体，让它看起来像是一场事故而不是谋杀。

73
01:08:35.000 --> 01:09:30.000
The two men reported the incident to police. When Gary Jubiland's team were once again investigating the case in 2007, they found a running sheet from April 1991 that detailed the men's sighting. But the information had never been properly investigated or made available at the trial for Clinton's murder. The original detectives hadn't even obtained formal statements from Greg and Michael. In 2016, Michael Scaffidi shared another detail with the journalist at Dandbox. A couple of years after he'd observed the strange scene at Norco Corner, he had been at work when some colleagues began passing around photographs from a community event in Bowerville.
这两个人向警方报告了这一事件。当加里·朱巴隆的团队在2007年再次调查此案时，他们发现了一张来自1991年4月的行动记录表，其中详细记录了这些人的目击情况。但这些信息从未得到适当的调查，也没有在克林顿谋杀案的审判中提供。最初的侦探甚至没有从格雷格和迈克尔那里获得正式证词。2016年，迈克尔·斯卡菲迪与《达恩博克斯》的记者分享了另一个细节。在他观察到诺科角诡异场景几年后，他在上班时，一些同事开始传阅鲍尔维尔一次社区活动的相片。

74
01:09:30.000 --> 01:10:27.000
Michael was looking at the photos when one person in a picture caught his eye. He asked his coworkers if they knew who the person was, and they flipped the photo over to read some names that had been scribbled on the back. According to these annotations, the person Michael had noticed was Jay Hart. Michael was certain that Hart was the man he'd seen with the indigenous boy at Norco Corner years earlier. Detective Jubiland and his team believed that the Norco Corner sighting constituted fresh and compelling evidence. On behalf of the New South Wales police force, they made a submission that Hart be retried for the murders of Clinton and Evelyn
迈克尔正在看照片时，照片中的一个人引起了他的注意。他问同事是否知道这个人是谁，他们把照片翻过来阅读写在背后的几个名字。根据这些注释，迈克尔注意到的那个人是杰伊·哈特。迈克尔确信哈特就是他多年前在诺科角与那个土著男孩在一起的那个男人。朱巴隆侦探和他的团队认为，诺科角目击事件构成了新的且令人信服的证据。他们代表新南威尔士州警察部队提交了一份意见书，要求对哈特进行克林顿和伊芙琳谋杀案的重新审判，

75
01:10:27.000 --> 01:11:22.000
and indicted for the murder of Colleen Craig. But on June 4, 2007, the DPP advised that the new evidence wasn't sufficiently fresh or compelling. Their application was denied. Over the years, the lack of answers and resolution in the three Bowerville murders has attracted attention from the media. The case has been featured in a number of high-profile television programs and was the subject of a 2013 documentary by Indigenous writer, legal academic and filmmaker Larissa Burrant. She travelled to Bowerville to interview the victims' families, and her film titled Innocence Betrayed won and was shortlisted for several awards.
并起诉谋杀科琳·克雷格。但在2007年6月4日，律政司通知说，新证据不够新或不够引人注目。他们的申请被拒绝了。多年来，鲍尔维尔三起谋杀案中缺乏答案和结果吸引了媒体的关注。该案已在许多备受瞩目的电视节目中播出，并成为土著作家、法律学者和电影制作人拉里萨·伯兰2013年纪录片的主题。她前往鲍尔维尔采访了受害者的家属，她名为《背叛的纯真》的电影赢得了多个奖项并入围决赛。

76
01:11:22.000 --> 01:12:12.000
Three years later, the Australian newspaper released a podcast series about the case. Crime journalist Dan Box interviewed Colleen, Evelyn and Clinton's families as well as various witnesses. He also spoke with Jay Hart at length. In their conversation, Hart, who has changed his name and no longer lives in Bowerville, strenuously denied having anything to do with the murders. He even stated that he wouldn't be opposed to being trialled again, as he believed it would provide him with the opportunity to clear his name once and for all. The series shone a new spotlight on the case and led to a renewed push for action.
三年后，《澳大利亚人报》发布了一系列关于此案的播客。犯罪记者丹·博克斯采访了科琳、伊芙琳和克林顿的家属以及各种证人。他还与杰伊·哈特进行了长谈。在他们的谈话中，已经改名且不再住在鲍尔维尔的哈特坚决否认与这些谋杀案有任何关系。他甚至表示，他不反对再次受审，因为他相信这会为他提供洗清自己罪名的一次机会。该系列节目为该案带来了新的聚光灯，并促使人们再次推动采取行动。

77
01:12:12.000 --> 01:13:17.000
As it turned out, the laws on admissibility of evidence had recently been updated, meaning that details of Colleen and Evelyn's cases would now be admissible in a trial for Clinton's murder. In February 2017, police charged Hart with Clinton and Evelyn's murders yet again. The New South Wales Attorney General applied to the state's court of criminal appeal for a retrial on the grounds that these new laws effectively gave rise to fresh and compelling evidence. The following year, this application was rejected, with the court ruling that none of the evidence was fresh. The Attorney General applied to Australia's High Court for special leave to appeal this decision, but was denied. To this day, Jay Hart maintains he had nothing to do with the murders of Evelyn Greenup or Clinton's speedy duro,
事实证明，关于证据可采性的法律最近已进行了更新，这意味着科琳和伊芙琳案件的细节现在将在审判克林顿谋杀案时具有可采性。2017年2月，警方再次以克林顿和伊芙琳谋杀案起诉哈特。新南威尔士州总检察长向该州的刑事上诉法院申请重新审判，理由是这些新法律有效地产生了新的且令人信服的证据。第二年，这一申请被驳回，法院裁定所有证据都不是新的。总检察长向澳大利亚高等法院申请特别许可对这一决定提出上诉，但遭到拒绝。直到今天，杰伊·哈特坚称他与伊芙琳·格林纳普或克林顿·斯皮迪·杜罗的谋杀案无关，

